{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018hGUGQNedQiei3UmDMv4Sh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * libtinyfseq v3.2.0 (2024-05-19)\n3\t * https://github.com/Cryptkeeper/libtinyfseq\n4\t * MIT License\n5\t *\n6\t * `TINYFSEQ_IMPLEMENTATION` should be defined in a SINGLE C/C++ source code file to include the function implementations.\n7\t * More information on using single-file libraries: https://github.com/nothings/stb#how-do-i-use-these-libraries\n8\t */\n9\t#ifndef TINYFSEQ_H\n10\t#define TINYFSEQ_H\n11\t\n12\t#include <stdint.h>\n13\t\n14\t#define TINYFSEQ_VERSION \"3.2.0\"\n15\t\n16\ttypedef enum tf_err_t {\n17\t    TF_OK = 0,\n18\t    TF_EINVALID_MAGIC,\n19\t    TF_EINVALID_COMPRESSION_TYPE,\n20\t    TF_EINVALID_BUFFER_SIZE,\n21\t    TF_EINVALID_VAR_SIZE,\n22\t} TFError;\n23\t\n24\t/**\n25\t * `TFError_string` returns a string version of the enum name, including a comment with additional error context.\n26\t * `TFError_string` does not allocate, its return values should not be freed.\n27\t *\n28\t * @param err Unknown/invalid values will default to returning \"unknown TFError value\"\n29\t * @return A string version of the given value, never NULL\n30\t */\n31\tconst char *TFError_string(TFError err);\n32\t\n33\ttypedef enum tf_compression_type_t {\n34\t    TF_COMPRESSION_NONE,\n35\t    TF_COMPRESSION_ZSTD,\n36\t    TF_COMPRESSION_ZLIB,\n37\t} TFCompressionType;\n38\t\n39\ttypedef struct tf_header_t {\n40\t    uint16_t channelDataOffset;\n41\t    uint8_t minorVersion;\n42\t    uint8_t majorVersion;\n43\t    uint16_t variableDataOffset;\n44\t    uint32_t channelCount;\n45\t    uint32_t frameCount;\n46\t    uint8_t frameStepTimeMillis;\n47\t    enum tf_compression_type_t compressionType;\n48\t    uint8_t compressionBlockCount;\n49\t    uint8_t channelRangeCount;\n50\t    uint64_t sequenceUid;\n51\t} TFHeader;\n52\t\n53\t/**\n54\t * `TFHeader_read` selectively decodes the fields available within `TFHeader` from a given data buffer.\n55\t * The buffer should be at least 32 bytes in length (the minimum size of a FSEQ v2.0+ header).\n56\t *\n57\t * @param bd Data buffer to decode into the given `TFHeader` pointer\n58\t * @param bs Size of the data buffer (>=32)\n59\t * @param header `TFHeader` instance to decode data buffer fields into\n60\t * @param ep End pointer which upon a successful return will point to the end of the structure within `bd` (may be NULL)\n61\t * @return A `TFError` value indicating an error, if any, otherwise `TF_OK`\n62\t */\n63\tTFError\n64\tTFHeader_read(const uint8_t *bd, int bs, TFHeader *header, uint8_t **ep);\n65\t\n66\ttypedef struct tf_compression_block_t {\n67\t    uint32_t firstFrameId;\n68\t    uint32_t size;\n69\t} TFCompressionBlock;\n70\t\n71\t/**\n72\t * `TFCompressionBlock_read` decodes the fields available within `TFCompressionBlock` from a given data buffer.\n73\t * The buffer should be at least 8 bytes in length (the fixed size of an encoded compression block).\n74\t *\n75\t * @param bd Data buffer to decode into the given `TFCompressionBlock` pointer\n76\t * @param bs Size of the data buffer (>=8)\n77\t * @param block `TFCompressionBlock` instance to decode data buffer fields into\n78\t * @param ep End pointer which upon a successful return will point to the end of the structure within `bd` (may be NULL)\n79\t * @return A `TFError` value indicating an error, if any, otherwise `TF_OK`\n80\t */\n81\tTFError TFCompressionBlock_read(const uint8_t *bd,\n82\t                                int bs,\n83\t                                TFCompressionBlock *block,\n84\t                                uint8_t **ep);\n85\t\n86\ttypedef struct tf_var_header_t {\n87\t    uint16_t size;\n88\t    uint8_t id[2];\n89\t} TFVarHeader;\n90\t\n91\t/**\n92\t * `TFVarHeader_read` decodes the fields available within `TFVarHeader` from a given data buffer.\n93\t * The buffer should be at least 5 bytes in length (the minimum size of an encoded variable header).\n9